<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="dark h-full bg-slate-950 text-slate-100">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0, viewport-fit=cover" />
  <title>How Nova Works — Transparency, Safety &amp; Data Controls | LLYVerse</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Plain-language guide to how Nova works on LLYVerse: capabilities, human approvals, guest widget limits, data retention, encrypted backups, and privacy controls." />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/tailwind.min.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/output.css" />
  <script src="/js/lucide.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body class="min-h-full flex flex-col bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 antialiased">
  <!-- Header -->
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-slate-800/80 bg-slate-950/85 backdrop-blur px-4 sm:px-6 h-16 flex items-center justify-between">
    <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-3">
      <img src="/favicon.svg" alt="LLYVerse Logo" class="w-8 h-8" />
      <span class="font-bold text-base text-white">LLYVerse <span class="text-xs font-mono text-cyan-400 ms-1">Nova Transparency</span></span>
    </a>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
      <a href="/privacy" class="px-3 py-2 rounded-xl bg-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-800 border border-slate-800 text-xs text-slate-300 transition min-h-[40px] flex items-center">
        Privacy Policy
      </a>
      <a href="/novaai" class="px-4 py-2 rounded-xl bg-cyan-700 hover:bg-cyan-800 text-white text-xs font-semibold transition min-h-[40px] flex items-center">
        Open Nova &rarr;
      </a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="flex-1 max-w-4xl w-full mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-10 space-y-8">
    <!-- Hero -->
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/30 text-cyan-300 text-xs font-mono">
        <i data-lucide="shield-check" class="w-3.5 h-3.5"></i>
        <span>Plain-Language Guide · Updated October 2026</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">How Nova Works</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Nova is LLYVerse’s multi-assistant workspace featuring three built-in personas — <strong>Nova</strong> (CEO &amp; Architect), <strong>Astra</strong> (Wonder &amp; Synthesis), and <strong>Astaria</strong> (Analyst &amp; Logic). This page explains in plain words what Nova can and cannot do, how your data is stored, and how you stay in control.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 1. What Nova Can and Cannot Do -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
        <i data-lucide="sparkles" class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400"></i>
        <span>1. What Nova Can &amp; Cannot Do</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
          <div class="font-bold text-cyan-300">What Nova Can Do</div>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>Maintain separate, persistent conversations per assistant (Nova, Astra, Astaria) and multi-agent Council rooms for signed-in members.</li>
            <li>Render formatted Markdown, code blocks, math formulas (KaTeX), and diagrams (Mermaid in strict sandboxed mode) using self-hosted vendor libraries.</li>
            <li>Remember facts you explicitly ask her to remember, and run scheduled routines on your behalf when enabled.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-slate-950 border border-slate-800 space-y-2">
          <div class="font-bold text-rose-300">What Nova Cannot Do</div>
          <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1">
            <li>Nova cannot run commands, overwrite or delete files, transfer Sparks or Flames, send emails, or write to databases without your explicit in-app confirmation.</li>
            <li>Nova never reads or logs raw passwords, API keys, or tokens entered into Secure Forms — those go straight into an AES-256-GCM encrypted vault.</li>
            <li>Nova cannot override the global <strong>Stop Nova</strong> kill switch.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 2. Human Approvals & Kill Switch (§15.1, §15.2) -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
        <i data-lucide="lock" class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400"></i>
        <span>2. How Approvals &amp; the Stop Switch Work</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        Before Nova takes any sensitive action (running a workspace command, modifying/deleting a file, transferring Sparks or Flames, making a payment, sending an outbound message, or writing to a database), she presents a <strong>Danger Approval Card</strong> showing the exact action details.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-xs text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong>Two-Click Human Confirmation:</strong> Danger actions require two deliberate clicks by a signed-in human user. Automated routines and background jobs can never self-approve.</li>
        <li><strong>Single-Use 5-Minute Tokens:</strong> Confirming an action mints a single-use token bound to the SHA-256 hash of the exact action payload. Tokens expire after <strong>5 minutes</strong> and cannot be reused or replayed.</li>
        <li><strong>Stop Nova Kill Switch:</strong> Clicking <strong>Stop Nova</strong> in the sidebar or info pane immediately cancels running tasks, closes live streams, revokes open approval tokens, and pauses scheduled routines.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 3. What Is Stored & Retention Periods -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
        <i data-lucide="database" class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400"></i>
        <span>3. What Is Stored &amp; For How Long</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-slate-800 text-slate-400 font-mono text-[11px] uppercase">
              <th class="py-2.5 pr-4">Data Type</th>
              <th class="py-2.5 pr-4">Where It Lives</th>
              <th class="py-2.5">Retention &amp; Control</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/70 text-slate-300">
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-white">Signed-In Chats &amp; Threads</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Account SQLite database</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Kept until you delete the conversation or account.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-white">Visible Memories</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Memory Vault (per-persona or shared)</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Editable and deletable anytime; "Forget everything" erases all memories immediately.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-white">Scheduled Routines</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Account routines table</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Kept until you pause or delete the routine.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-white">Activity Log (nova_actions)</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Append-only audit table</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Records tool calls, approvals, memory writes, and routine runs with all secrets redacted.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-white">Encrypted Nightly Backups</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4">AES-256-GCM archive outside web root</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Retained for <strong>14 days</strong>, then automatically pruned. Deleted data ages out within 14 days.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4 font-semibold text-white">Guest Widget Chats</td>
              <td class="py-2.5 pr-4">Browser tab session only (<code class="font-mono text-cyan-300">sessionStorage</code>)</td>
              <td class="py-2.5">Cleared as soon as you close the browser tab (can be imported once if you sign in).</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 4. Guest Widget Limits (§12) -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
        <i data-lucide="message-circle" class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400"></i>
        <span>4. Guest Widget Limits</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
        Visitors who are not signed in can try Nova using the floating widget on public pages. The full workspace (<code class="font-mono text-cyan-300">/novaai</code> and <code class="font-mono text-cyan-300">/app</code>) requires signing in.
      </p>
      <ul class="text-xs text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong>Nova Persona Only:</strong> Guests chat with Nova only (no Astra, Astaria, or multi-agent rooms).</li>
        <li><strong>Text Only:</strong> File uploads, attachments, voice memos, and secure forms are disabled for guests.</li>
        <li><strong>No Tools or Computer Access:</strong> Guest conversations run with all MCP connectors, tools, memory, routines, and computer actions turned off.</li>
        <li><strong>Rate &amp; Length Caps:</strong> Limited to <strong>10 messages per 10 minutes</strong> and <strong>30 messages per day</strong> per IP address, with replies capped at approximately <strong>500 tokens</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. How to Export or Delete Your Data (§15.4) -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
        <i data-lucide="trash-2" class="w-5 h-5 text-cyan-400"></i>
        <span>5. How to Export or Delete Your Data</span>
      </h2>
      <ul class="text-xs text-slate-300 list-disc list-inside space-y-1.5 leading-relaxed">
        <li><strong>Memory Vault:</strong> Open the Info Pane &rarr; <strong>Memory &rarr; Manage</strong> (or <strong>Settings &rarr; Memory &amp; Encrypted Backups</strong>) to search, edit, or delete individual memories.</li>
        <li><strong>Export JSON:</strong> Click <strong>Export JSON</strong> in the Memory Vault to download a complete copy of your saved memories.</li>
        <li><strong>Forget Everything:</strong> Click <strong>Forget Everything</strong> (two-click confirmation) to immediately delete all saved memories for your account. Deleted items age out of encrypted backups within <strong>14 days</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Delete Conversations:</strong> Right-click (or long-press on mobile) any conversation in the sidebar and choose <strong>Delete</strong>.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. Contact & Bug Reports -->
    <section class="bg-slate-900 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl p-6 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <div class="space-y-1">
        <h2 class="text-base font-bold text-white">Questions or Bug Reports?</h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">Reach out through the LLYVerse support &amp; bug report form or review our full Privacy Policy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5">
        <a href="/portal#contact" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-cyan-700 hover:bg-cyan-800 text-white text-xs font-semibold transition min-h-[44px] flex items-center">
          Report a Bug / Contact Support
        </a>
        <a href="/terms" class="px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-200 text-xs font-medium transition min-h-[44px] flex items-center">
          Terms of Service
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <%- include('partials/legal_footer') %>
  <script>
    if (window.lucide) lucide.createIcons();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
